The TK interface could be completely mouse driven if it weren't for
the ackwardness of moving your character with the mouse.  Icons and
pull down menus and life/magic/food bars easily readable, automatic
log keeping browsable database of all items, monsters, and people met
(think Pokedex..lol), even equipping your hero was simple as dragging
objects from inventory to a picture of your character and it would put
it to the closest viable slot, etc....it's probably against everything
that hardcore roguelike players want or will respect, but it would
definately broaden the user base of this genre if more games had the
sort of interface it has.  And you could still play it with just the
keyboard if you wanted.  The regular Angband and variants are more
akin to NetHack's window port with the option of customizing (to a
very small extent) a few extra windows to various things.  

